[
  {
    "sha": "b85e5d77decdbfc9857f07f38ba56cd53badf1c1",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGI4NWU1ZDc3ZGVjZGJmYzk4NTdmMDdmMzhiYTU2Y2Q1M2JhZGYxYzE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T20:59:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T20:59:53Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): export and import the document's tools as a tool library file\n\nThe Tool library page gains \"Export library...\" and \"Import library...\".\nExport writes every document tool as camcraft-tools/1 JSON ({format,\nversion, units: mm, tools: [{name, definition}]}), each definition the\nexact tool shape MCP's get_job/add_tool and the project file already use.\nImport (app::tool_library::parse_tool_library + commands::ImportTools) is\none undo unit: the whole file is validated first - malformed JSON, a\nwrong format/version, a missing field, a name twice, a reserved name or a\ntool Tool::is_sane refuses each refuse the import by tool name with\nnothing applied. A name already in the document is never overwritten: an\nidentical tool is skipped, a different one comes in as \"<name> (2)\".\nVendor library formats stay out of scope (clean-room).\n\nRefs #300\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
